# Freebuff local dev-tool artifacts (SQLite state, lImplement proper project member management and ownership controls in DevSync.

First inspect the existing project membership, invitation, notification, team chat and authorization implementation. Do not create a separate permission system. Reuse the existing backend entities, APIs, services and project membership logic.

CURRENT ISSUE:
The Project → Members page shows all members and their roles, but there is no action available for the project owner to manage members.

IMPLEMENT THIS FLOW:

1. PROJECT OWNER MEMBER ACTIONS

On:
Project → Members

For every member except the current owner, show a 3-dot action menu.

Menu options:

- Remove from Project
- Promote to Owner

Only the current project owner can see and use these actions.

Normal members must NOT see these owner-only controls.

2. REMOVE MEMBER

When owner selects:

Remove from Project

show a confirmation modal:

"Remove member?"

"Are you sure you want to remove @username from this project?"

Buttons:
Cancel
Remove Member

After confirmation:

- Remove the user from project membership.
- Remove their access to the project.
- They must no longer be able to access:
  - Overview
  - Board
  - Tasks
  - Team Chat
  - Files
  - Docs
  - Members
  - Activity
  - Project Settings
- Remove them from the project's team chat/group.
- Remove their pending project-related permissions if applicable.
- Create an activity entry such as:
  "Owner removed @username from the project."
- Send a notification to the removed user explaining that they were removed from the project.

Do NOT delete the user's DevSync account.
Do NOT delete their personal messages.
Do NOT delete unrelated projects or data.

3. TEAM CHAT REMOVAL

When a member is removed from a project:

They must automatically lose access to that project's team chat.

They must no longer appear in the project team chat member list.

They must not be able to send new messages to that project chat.

Existing project messages should remain intact for the remaining members.

Do NOT delete the entire chat history.

4. PROMOTE MEMBER TO OWNER

Owner should have:

"Transfer Ownership"

instead of directly changing ownership without confirmation.

When selected, show:

"Transfer project ownership?"

"@username will become the new project owner. You will lose owner permissions."

Buttons:
Cancel
Transfer Ownership

After confirmation:

- Change project owner to the selected member.
- Previous owner becomes a normal member.
- New owner receives owner permissions.
- Previous owner loses owner-only permissions.
- Update the Members page immediately.
- Create an activity entry:
  "Project ownership transferred from @oldOwner to @newOwner."
- Send notifications to both users.

IMPORTANT:
There must always be exactly ONE project owner.

Do not allow:
- Owner removing themselves.
- Owner transferring ownership to a non-member.
- Multiple owners.
- Normal members transferring ownership.
- Removed users becoming owner.

5. BACKEND AUTHORIZATION

Do NOT rely only on frontend hiding buttons.

Every owner-only backend endpoint must verify:

Authenticated user
↓
Project membership
↓
Authenticated user is CURRENT project owner
↓
Perform action

A normal member must receive an appropriate 403 response when attempting owner-only actions through the API.

Also verify that a removed member cannot access the project by directly calling project APIs or manually entering project URLs.

6. MEMBERS PAGE UI

Improve the existing Members page without redesigning the whole application.

Keep the existing DevSync design system.

For each member show:

Avatar
Name
Username
Join date
Role badge
3-dot actions menu where authorized

Example:

Tushar Dhiman
@tushar97
Joined about 4 hours ago
OWNER

Chat Fix
@chatfix
Joined about 2 hours ago
MEMBER
                                      ⋮

Nakul Sharma
@nakul97
Joined about 4 hours ago
MEMBER
                                      ⋮

The 3-dot menu should be keyboard accessible.

Add proper aria-label:
"Member actions"

7. OWNER PROTECTION

The owner should not have a Remove option for themselves.

The owner can only transfer ownership to another existing project member.

If ownership is transferred, update all UI and authorization checks immediately.

8. NOTIFICATIONS

Use the existing notification system.

Create notifications for:

- Member removed from project
- Ownership transferred
- Optional: ownership transfer received

Do not create a new notification architecture.

9. ACTIVITY LOG

Use the existing Activity system.

Record:

- Member removed
- Ownership transferred

Activity should contain:
Actor
Target user
Project
Action
Timestamp

10. TEAM CHAT

Reuse the existing project team-chat implementation.

When removing a member, update chat membership using the existing chat/group architecture.

Do not create a separate chat system.

11. SECURITY TESTS

Add/update backend integration tests for:

- Owner can remove member
- Owner cannot remove themselves
- Normal member cannot remove another member
- Normal member cannot call remove-member API
- Owner can transfer ownership
- Normal member cannot transfer ownership
- Ownership transfer creates exactly one owner
- Previous owner becomes MEMBER
- New owner becomes OWNER
- Removed member cannot access project
- Removed member cannot access project team chat
- Removed member cannot send messages to project team chat
- Existing members retain access
- Existing chat messages remain intact

12. FRONTEND TESTS

Verify:

- Owner sees member action menu.
- Normal member does not see owner controls.
- Remove confirmation modal works.
- Cancel works.
- Successful removal updates member list.
- Transfer ownership confirmation works.
- Successful ownership transfer updates roles.
- Loading states work.
- API errors show user-friendly messages.
- No duplicate requests occur.

13. IMPORTANT DATA SAFETY

Do NOT delete:

- User accounts
- User profiles
- Other projects
- Personal messages
- Existing project messages
- Existing tasks
- Existing files
- Existing docs
- Existing activity history

Only modify project membership/authorization and related project-chat membership.

Finally run:

- Backend unit tests
- Backend integration tests
- Frontend tests
- TypeScript check
- Production build

Fix any errors introduced by this implementation.

At the end report:
1. Files modified
2. APIs added/modified
3. Database changes
4. Authorization changes
5. Member removal flow
6. Ownership transfer flow
7. Team chat changes
8. Notification changes
9. Tests passed
10. Build resultogs, tokens)
